# Oracle Consensus Engine

## Purpose

The Oracle Consensus Engine measures where elite Polymarket traders independently agree.

The engine evaluates:

- Number of active traders
- Capital committed
- Trader specialization
- Position conviction
- Timing
- Market category

The output is an Oracle Score between 0 and 100.

Higher scores indicate stronger evidence of elite consensus.
# Oracle Scoring Model v1

## Formula

Oracle Score =
35% Consensus
25% Capital
20% Trader Quality
10% Conviction
10% Freshness

---

Consensus

How many elite traders agree?

---

Capital

Total money committed.

---

Trader Quality

Leaderboard rank and historical performance.

---

Conviction

Large positions increase confidence.

---

Freshness

Recent entries receive higher weight.
